# The agency's own WATSTORE peak files are frozen as reference bytes and
# their content hashes are recorded in the fixtures beside them. They
# carry CRLF line endings as the service serves them, so git must not
# normalise them: a normalised copy is no longer the file that was
# fetched, and the hash it is checked against would be a hash of our own
# rewriting.
verification/fixtures/peaks/*_reference.txt -text
